From the Democratic Party's big wins in the US midterm elections to France's ongoing student-led protests and the first Olympic sports event held on African soil, FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6cb3870-db7e-11f1-a1cc-330d38f8a0f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:21:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/32d96078-db74-11f1-b6c9-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26310471490191.jpg">© Kieran Cleeves, OIS/IOC via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. FRANCE 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5cea55f2-db7e-11f1-bd0a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-150134-150232-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">620ad868-db7e-11f1-9f57-c1ea51b6f7a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:21:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac245178-db7d-11f1-9478-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140118-140318-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b127f486-db7d-11f1-8be9-85907240b2be</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:18:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says</link><description>
France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3ba58f6-db7a-11f1-9002-631a5aa7e06e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:16:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57d3784e-db7b-11f1-a752-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-31T022255Z-1628715710-RC2ZDOAFTXRB-RTRMADP-3-G20-MINISTERS-1.jpg">© Megan Varner, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Poland launches terrorism probe into mass shooting in Krakow</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting</link><description>
Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c557d2b2-db52-11f1-9660-1f24a097f366</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 08:59:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1250eae-db5d-11f1-9d08-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/df1b226879aa9026b8f83a806b14523cef6d3728.jpg">© Wojtek Radwanski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gunman kills six in Krakow, three more bodies found at his house</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house</link><description>
A chilling new discovery in Poland, where three bodies have reportedly been found inside the Krakow gunman's home. That's in addition to six people killed and sixteen wounded when the attacker opened fire in the city's historic square. Prime Minister Donald Tusk has now declared the shooting an act of terrorism, saying Poland has never experienced anything quite like it. The 25-year-old suspect, described by authorities as holding radical far-right views, was shot by police. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3454c354-daeb-11f1-8b85-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311723511956.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3454c354-daeb-11f1-8b85-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311723511956.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4df2c178-daf8-11f1-a44d-c7e09584ebf8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 22:47:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Gunman who killed at least six in Krakow ‘fascinated’ by far-right ideologies, government says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-at-least-three-people-killed-shooting-in-polish-city-of-krakow-police-say</link><description>
A gunman reportedly "fascinated by far-right ideologies" shot and killed at least six people and wounded more than a dozen in Krakow’s main market square on Saturday, Polish authorities said. Three more bodies were later found at the home of the gunman, who was wounded and taken into custody.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3454c354-daeb-11f1-8b85-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311723511956.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3454c354-daeb-11f1-8b85-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311723511956.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a362e96-dabe-11f1-8c51-ed9627d42fd2</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 15:23:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3454c354-daeb-11f1-8b85-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26311723511956.jpg">© Beata Zawrze, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia launches massive strike on Kyiv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261107-russia-launches-massive-strike-on-kyiv-1</link><description>
As Ukraine prepares for another round of talks with Russia and the United States next week, Moscow has launched a massive overnight strike. At least five people were injured in Kyiv, where Russian missiles damaged residential and commercial buildings, forced the closure of a bridge over the Dnipro River and caused fresh power and water outages. Ophélie Jacobson reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50e433a2-daa4-11f1-b5c1-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120558-120735-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/50e433a2-daa4-11f1-b5c1-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-120558-120735-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55cbc560-daa4-11f1-b87b-8911991cdc94</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 12:15:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>AI Data centres face growing backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ai-data-centres-face-growing-backlash</link><description>
Democrats are also calling for tighter regulation of AI data centres, a concern shared across Europe. In Amsterdam, several hundred activists occupied the site of a planned Microsoft data centre as part of a two-day protest taking place across the continent. Jennie Shin reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b12b7e0-da8e-11f1-96c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-100946-101139-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b12b7e0-da8e-11f1-96c8-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261107-100946-101139-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80584c60-da8e-11f1-af87-a90c70a6f21e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:39:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia hits Kyiv and surrounding region in massive overnight strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261107-moscow-strikes-kyiv-as-ukraine-prepares-for-talks-with-russia-and-the-us</link><description>
Moscow ⁠carried out missile ​and drone attacks on Kyiv and the surrounding region overnight Friday to Saturday, targeting energy infrastructure and killing at least one person while wounding eight, authorities said. Russia recently stepped up air strikes on ​Ukraine, worsening living conditions for residents who have limited access to power and water.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/546cb698-da81-11f1-a20b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T070706Z-606536925-RC2OIOAD7FJI-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/546cb698-da81-11f1-a20b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T070706Z-606536925-RC2OIOAD7FJI-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d47f682-da81-11f1-bf51-7bf324691a66</guid><pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:08:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/546cb698-da81-11f1-a20b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-07T070706Z-606536925-RC2OIOAD7FJI-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Gleb Garanich, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe bomb hoaxes widen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-bomb-hoaxes-widen</link><description>
The series of hoax bomb scares sent to several Irish media outlets and European airlines are likely part of a coordinated campaign of disruption, according to the Irish government. Dozens of commercial flights have been targetted by email with threats said to be over and above the typical hoax in specificty. Ireland's broadcaster RTE who's staff evacuated the premises this morning and several Italian airlines, say they received a mesage cliaming to be from a Russian extremist group calling itself the Fighters of the Male State, which denied its implication. France 24's Jean-Emile Jammine speaks to Eric Schouten, founder and CEO of Dyami Security Intelligence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4fadc82-da26-11f1-bdcc-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2027abfe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4fadc82-da26-11f1-bdcc-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-2027abfe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1932fd32-da25-11f1-8828-79379f6052bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 21:22:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>What Trump’s midterms debacle could mean for US support for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-what-trump-s-midterms-debacle-could-mean-for-us-support-for-ukraine</link><description>
The Republican Party's crushing defeat in midterm elections has left Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky optimistic about future support for Kyiv and stronger transatlantic relations. But with US President Donald Trump retaining broad foreign policy powers, the Democratic majority in Congress may have limited scope to bring about substantial change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da1effc4-d9de-11f1-837c-91cdb8d44ed0</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:49:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4dcb4de-d9de-11f1-b426-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-24T100014Z-973605904-RC2HONATRV49-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP-ZELENSKIY-RELATIONSHIP.jpg">© Kylie Cooper, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Europe: What we know about the hoax bomb threats disrupting flights</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe-what-we-know-about-the-hoax-bomb-threats-disrupting-flights</link><description>
Dozens of European flights have been disrupted this week after bomb threats were sent in to various airports, with fighter planes escorting many civilian aircraft after threats were called in mid-flight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/821a507a-da02-11f1-960f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/821a507a-da02-11f1-960f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/Thumb-01-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97255028-da02-11f1-bb76-5534a78b8157</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:59:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>British comedian Russell Brand found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-british-comedian-russell-brand-found-guilty-of-rape-and-three-sexual-assaults</link><description>
British comedian Russell Brand was on Thursday, November 5, found guilty of rape and three sexual assaults by a London jury, including for an incident involving a 16-year-old girl. He now faces "significant" prison time, according to the judge. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/090853f4-da01-11f1-95a1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b57246d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/090853f4-da01-11f1-95a1-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b57246d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1dad8d2-da00-11f1-ad93-c33636d1bed4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:45:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'Trump is a very dangerous person for the world': EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-trump-is-a-very-dangerous-person-for-the-world-eu-s-former-top-diplomat-josep-borrell</link><description>
In an interview with Talking Europe, the EU's former top diplomat Josep Borrell reacts to the Democrats' victory in the US midterm elections, warning that US President Donald Trump is still "a very dangerous person for the world".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1462964-d9f1-11f1-8b86-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-JOSEP-BORRELL-1.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d1462964-d9f1-11f1-8b86-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-JOSEP-BORRELL-1.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b329fcd4-d6af-11f1-af0c-4789fb9a1a2f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:44:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Chaos within aviation industry' as European air traffic hit by bomb threats</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261106-chaos-within-aviation-industry-as-european-air-traffic-hit-by-bomb-threats</link><description>
Officials across Europe reported a fresh slew of bomb threats against multiple flights on Friday, November 6, following a string of hoaxes that have caused flight diversions this week. Two broadcasters also received security threats, in a possible sign the menace was spreading beyond the skies. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1649d436-d9ff-11f1-b43d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5cd1fe0d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1649d436-d9ff-11f1-b43d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5cd1fe0d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96eb94c8-d9fd-11f1-8429-d76a332baec9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:33:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>Europe's crisis of discontent: Student and cost-of-living protests spread across EU</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261106-europe-s-crisis-of-discontent-student-and-cost-of-living-protests-spread-across-eu</link><description>
A growing wave of discontent is sweeping across Europe. What began in France as student protests over deteriorating school conditions, teacher shortages and an education system under pressure has quickly grown into something much bigger: a groundswell of discontent over the rising cost of living, unaffordable housing and struggling public services.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28d69d38-d922-11f1-bb94-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-DEBAT-EN-2.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28d69d38-d922-11f1-bb94-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-DEBAT-EN-2.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5efb6fa2-d6b0-11f1-909b-3551a7733bb3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:48:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French 2027 presidential elections: Why Mélenchon is a Gen Z favourite</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-2027-presidential-elections-why-melenchon-is-a-gen-z-favourite</link><description>
Hard-left presidential candidate Jean-Luc Mélenchon is beloved by French youth, but also one of the country’s most controversial politicians. His encouragement of the youth protests sweeping through France months ahead of the presidential election has only made him more divisive. So, why is Mélenchon a Gen Z favourite? FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler spoke to young supporters to find out.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29fed0fa-d9d5-11f1-accf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/New-TITLE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29fed0fa-d9d5-11f1-accf-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/New-TITLE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c270b52-d9d5-11f1-8b28-5774d120281e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 11:43:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Death toll rises to 50 in Russian attack on aid distribution ‌point in Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261106-death-toll-rises-to-50-in-russian-attack-on-aid-distribution-point-in-ukraine</link><description>
The death toll from Russia's bombing of an aid ​distribution ‌point in ⁠Ukraine's southeastern Zaporizhzhia region on Monday ‌has risen to 50, Kyiv's Emergency Service said on Friday, making it ​one of the deadliest strikes ‌on civilians this year. 
